</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §2 Hierarchical Specialization -->
<section id="s-hierarchy" data-code="hierarchy">
<div class="section-no">02 — Hierarchical Specialization</div>
<h2>Decomposing the data science lifecycle</h2>
<p>
  Flattening all actions into a single agent forces the model to choose from an overly large, complex tool space, which dramatically increases tool-selection errors. EvoDS implements a <strong>Hierarchical Multi-Agent Architecture</strong> that separates concern areas.
</p>
<p>
  At the top, the <strong>Manager Agent</strong> acts as the global orchestrator. It inspects the environment, divides the main problem into smaller subtasks, and delegates them to specialized lower-level agents. Lower-level sub-agents maintain localized action spaces:
</p>

