  By partitioning the available operations, EvoDS reduces the action space size of each agent node. Mathematically, the paper proves in <strong>Theorem 5.1</strong> that the upper bound on the tool-selection error probability of this hierarchical routing is strictly lower than that of a flat agent architecture.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §3 Autonomous Skill Acquisition -->
<section id="s-asa" data-code="asa">
<div class="section-no">03 — Autonomous Skill Acquisition</div>
<h2>How agents learn new actions from experience</h2>
<p>
  When a subtask exceeds the capability of a sub-agent's basic tools, the sub-agent is allowed to synthesize a new tool. This is the <strong>Autonomous Skill Acquisition (ASA)</strong> mechanism, which operates in four distinct phases:
</p>

<div class="step-list">
  <div class="step-box active" data-step="0">
    <div class="step-num">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Synthesis: On-Demand Creation</div>
      <div class="step-desc">The sub-agent generates a structured skill candidate consisting of a name, detailed execution description, and raw parameterized Python code.</div>
      <div class="step-code">def imbalanced_classification_smote(X, y): ...</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" data-step="1">
    <div class="step-num">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Verification: Environment Testing</div>
      <div class="step-desc">The generated code is executed within the sandbox. The execution results are analyzed for syntactical correctness and outcome validity. Failed code is discarded.</div>
      <div class="step-code">Execution check: Exit Code 0, Output Valid.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" data-step="2">
    <div class="step-num">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Caching: Synthesized Repository</div>
      <div class="step-desc">Successful skills are stored in a temporary synthesized skill repository. The model keeps a usage-frequency counter for each cached candidate.</div>
      <div class="step-code">Candidate pool candidate_skills.add(smote_skill, count=1)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="step-box" data-step="3">
    <div class="step-num">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-title">Expansion: Permanent Merge</div>
      <div class="step-desc">If a cached skill is synthesized repeatedly (usage count &gt;= 3), indicating a recurring task requirement, it is permanently added to the agent's action space.</div>
      <div class="step-code">Permanent Action Space merged: A_modeler = A_modeler ∪ &#123;smote_skill&#125;</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

