  <button id="step-next">Next Step</button>
  <span class="step-prog-label" id="step-prog">Step 1 of 4</span>
</div>

<p>
  During experiments, EvoDS synthesized a total of <strong>279 skills</strong>, which were invoked 925 times. This represents a <strong>69% cross-task skill reuse rate</strong>, proving that the agent successfully abstracts reusable abstractions rather than task-specific procedures.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §4 Adaptive Context Compression -->
<section id="s-acc" data-code="acc">
<div class="section-no">04 — Adaptive Context Compression</div>
<h2>Mitigating the lost-in-the-middle effect</h2>
<p>
  Instead of passively truncating history (which deletes important intermediate insights), EvoDS implements <strong>Adaptive Context Compression (ACC)</strong> at two separate levels:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Sub-agent Level:</strong> Raw execution trace logs, Pandas debug readouts, and compilation backtraces are condensed by the sub-agent into a short summary before being sent back to the Manager Agent.</li>
  <li><strong>Manager Level:</strong> The Manager Agent is equipped with a learned compression tool: <code>context_summarize</code>. It decides <em>when</em> to trigger context summarization dynamically based on the current context complexity.</li>
</ul>

