<p>
  By actively calling the summarization tool, the Manager compresses historical logs, keeping the active context size bounded. In the paper, <strong>Theorem 5.2</strong> theoretically shows that the Manager's compression objective aligns with the <strong>Information Bottleneck principle</strong>, which minimizes task-irrelevant signals while preserving task-critical outputs.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §5 Agentic GRPO -->
<section id="s-rl" data-code="grpo">
<div class="section-no">05 — Joint Reinforcement Learning</div>
<h2>Co-training Manager and sub-agent behaviors</h2>
<p>
  To optimize task coordination, skill selection, and context compression, EvoDS uses <strong>Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)</strong>. GRPO allows training a group of rollouts without the overhead of an auxiliary critic network.
</p>
<p>
  The training objective co-optimizes the Manager Agent and the sub-agents. The overall reward formulation for the Manager Agent is structured as a hybrid combination of solution quality and execution cost:
</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">Manager Agent Reward Formulation</div>
  <span class="math-var">R_main</span> = <span class="math-var">R_outcome</span> + 0.2 <span class="math-op">*</span> <span class="math-var">R_sub</span> - 0.1 <span class="math-op">*</span> <span class="math-var">P_context</span> - 0.1 <span class="math-op">*</span> <span class="math-var">P_turn</span>
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment"># Where:</span>
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment"># R_outcome ∈ [0, 1] is the final benchmark evaluation score</span>
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment"># R_sub is the average success rate of delegated subtasks</span>
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment"># P_context = |C| / C_max is the token usage context penalty</span>
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment"># P_turn = T / T_max is the turn usage efficiency penalty</span>
</div>

<p>
  This joint reward function penalizes agents that solve tasks inefficiently by generating overly long contexts or wasting coordination turns, directly aligning model policy with the information bottleneck objective.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §6 Benchmarks -->
